# Task 12 — AOSS Retrieval: Cold-Start + Tenant Isolation Proof (ACC-4)

Architect-executed 2026-07-09/10 (witnessed, dev 697114252993).
Tooling: AossProverFn (VPC-attached ops Lambda, this task) invoking the REAL
production retrieve() wrapper — proof exercises the exact code agents will run.

## 0. Carry fixed first: retrieval client was UNSIGNED (Task-11 live 403)

retrieval.ts's default client was a bare fetch (no SigV4) — every AOSS query
from a deployed Lambda 403'd. Fix: SigV4 machinery extracted from
aoss-apply-template.ts into shared/aoss-signed-client.ts (single-source signing,
REV-10 discipline); retrieval defaultAossClient now signs (service 'aoss',
x-amz-content-sha256). Regression pinned: default-client test asserts
AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 + /aoss/aws4_request headers on the wire.

## 1. Infrastructure (deployed + cloud-read-back)

- AossProverFn: VPC-attached (2 subnets), 120s, actions template-check / seed /
  query(→retrieve()) / search-control / delete-index. ONE-DOOR intact: no
  bedrock:* on its role (unit-asserted); vectors arrive in payloads only.
  Index guard: mutations refused unless index prefixed task12-/task13-/task14-.
- Data-access policy (read back live): READ = invoker + 8 handlers;
  WRITE = seeder + apply-template; prover = own block (see §5 defect).

