## 4. Cold-start budget (45s, REQ-RET-3) — DEMONSTRATED, with honest deviation

DEVIATION from deliverable wording: dev AOSS does NOT scale to literal zero.
Witnessed: SearchOCU/IndexingOCU flat at 0.5/0.5 for 6+ idle hours pre-proof
AND through the active proof (CloudWatch, ClientId=697114252993, 17:00Z→00:20Z
all datapoints avg=max=0.5). Config: VECTORSEARCH, standbyReplicas=DISABLED —
0.5 OCU is the AOSS floor for this posture. "Wait for scale-to-zero" is
unachievable in this account; the equivalent honest proof is first-query-after-idle:

- After 6h+ idle: first data-plane hit 1.59s wall (template GET, incl. Lambda
  cold start).
- After a witnessed 50-min zero-data-plane idle window (23:25:17Z→00:15:17Z,
  timer-enforced): timed retrieve() at 00:15:34Z → latencyMs=557, attempts=1,
  results identical & correct (A1/A2/A3, all tenant-a).
- 45s budget headroom ≈ 80×. Backoff machinery (500ms base → 45s ceiling)
  additionally unit-proven (retries on 503, AossColdStartTimeoutError at ceiling).

## 5. Live-found defect during cleanup (fixed + deployed + test-pinned)

delete-index → HTTP 403 authorization_exception: the shared WRITE block lacked
aoss:DeleteIndex. Fix: prover moved to its OWN data-access rule block with
DeleteIndex; seeder/apply-template deliberately do NOT gain it (least
privilege). Unit test pins DeleteIndex appears exactly once and only for the
prover. Deployed (45/45 infra tests), delete retried → {"deleted":"task12-e2e",
"status":200}; deletion visibility also async (~60s) — GONE (404) confirmed
00:19:04Z.

